Hello,
We happen to be looking for a filesystem project for our undergrad project
and after looking into your pool of ideas did like the time-machine like
browser, time slider and definitely the B-tree based directory management.

Though the first two ideas are very promising and the simplicity with which
one can get the system back to one's desired time frame, looking into as a
years work doesn't cut it.

And as I see the b-tree based directory management under the long term to do
list, I wish to know the feasibility of it for undergrads. And if yes which
path must be begin with to learn as well come up with a solution worth
giving back to the community.

We eagerly await for your kind reply.

Thank you.

P.S: We are looking for kernel based projects.
-- 
Prasenjit Giri

